# R1 research: the claim does not exist

Lead: There is no claim to research. The task brief pointed at discussion/claims/.claude/, which is not
 a claim: it never contained a claim.md, was never committed to git, and was a leftover artifact directory of the Claude Code adjudicator CLI. This round documents that finding and
 the fix that landed while this round was in flight.

Method: evidence gathered 2026-11-24 11:30-11:36 CET on the harness, from the repo
 tree at commit bf7b55d/d94a184 (main) and the Claude Code session transcripts in ~/.claude/projects
/. No external sources; no web; no database. Population for every figure = this repo's tree and this machine's Claude Code session logs
, as of the timestamps given.

## 1. The finding

| # | Fact | Population / sample | Source |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1.1 | The claim directory named in the brief, discussion/claims/.claude/, never contained a claim.md. At 2026-
11-24 11:29 CET it held exactly one entry: the empty directory .cc-writes/ (drwx------). No title, no falsifier, no claim text existed to
 research. | 1 directory, fully listed (2 entries incl. . and ..) | ls -la discussion/claims/.claude
/, run 2026-11-24 ~11:31 CET |
| 1.2 | The directory was never tracked by git: git ls-files discussion/claims/.claude returned
 nothing, and no commit in the repo's history touches it. | whole git history of the repo at d
94a184 | git ls-files + git log --all, 2026-11-24 ~11:31 |
| 1.3 | The repo's own .gitignore declares the truth: `.claude/` with the comment "Claude CLI working artifacts - never claims, never committed"
 (line 11-12). bin/next and bin/reindex contradicted this by scanning every directory under discussion/claims/
 with os.listdir, which includes hidden dirs. | 1 gitignore rule; 2 tools | .gitignore:12; bin/next:214
,272; bin/reindex:30 |
| 1.4 | Because bin/next sorts claim directories with os.listdir, ".claude" (ASCII 46
) sorted before every Cxxx claim (ASCII 67) and was picked FIRST every dispatch cycle. The loop dispatched a researcher round (this one) against "(untitled)" at
 [11:30] round 3/7. | 1 dispatch cycle, rounds log | bin/next:214,272-274; discussion/rounds/2026-11
-24-harness-nflinv.log:116-119 |
| 1.5 | Origin: Claude Code session f6b97ac8 (the C003 adjudicator round, claude-sonnet-5-5,
 logged [11:29] round 2/7) ran 8 tool calls with cwd /home/dennis/nflinventory/discussion/claims. The CLI drops
 a hidden .claude/.cc-writes marker in its cwd; the directory's mtime (2026-11-24 11:29:01 CET) matches that
 session's window. The sibling session 06a89794 (C002 verdict) shows the same artifact in discussion/.claude/ (
mtime 11:29:01). | 2 Claude Code session transcripts (~/.claude/projects/-home-dennis-nflinventory/), 47-52
 recorded cwd values each | grep '"cwd"' over the transcripts, run 2026-11-24 ~11:34 |
| 1.6 | The same artifact exists wherever the CLI ran: /home/dennis/nflinventory/.cla
ude/.cc-writes (2026-11-22 04:00), bin/.claude/.cc-writes (2026-11-21 21:16), discussion/.
claude/.cc-writes (2026-11-24 11:29). | 4 artifact dirs on this machine | find /home/dennis/nflinventory -name .
cc-writes, 2026-11-24 ~11:32 |

## 2. The fix that landed while this round was in flight

- Commit 96dbe7e (2026-11-24 11:32:52, "bin/next: the claim scan only accepts Cxxx directories; gitignore .claude/")
 added the Cxxx filter to bin/next:276 and the .gitignore rule. Its commit message independently documents the same diagnosis ("
one wasted round proved it" — that round is this one).
- The stray directory was deleted from disk at 11:32 (claims dir mtime 11:32); the index no longer lists it
.
- bin/next now dispatches C005 adjudicator round 3; "7 claims in flight" (down from the 9 the brief showed, which counted the phantom and pre
-settle C002/C003/C007).

## 3. What is still open (genuine gap)

- bin/reindex:30 still scans with bare os.listdir and no Cxxx filter. If another tool
ing directory appears under discussion/claims/, the index will again list a phantom open claim with a dead
 link (as it did between 11:29 and 11:32: index generated 2026-11-24 showed "[.claude .claude](claims
/.claude/claim.md) | open | - | - | 0"). bin/drift:89 and bin/backlog:49 are safe: both filter on frontmatter contents, so a directory without claim.md
 is skipped.
- The gate would refuse any round filed here anyway (bin/gate-independence shape(): claim directory must match ^C\d+
...), so this round is a record, not a counted round.

## 4. Falsifier (the brief asked for one)

Finding: "discussion/claims/.claude was a stray Claude Code CLI artifact, never a claim." Falsified
 if: evidence that the directory ever held a claim.md created by bin/claim, or that any
 git commit contained a claim.md under it. As of 2026-11-24 11:36 CET: no such evidence exists in the repo's history (checked 1.2) or on
 disk (checked 1.1 before the directory was deleted).

## 5. Recommendation

- Add the same Cxxx filter to bin/reindex:30 (one line, mirrors bin/next:276). Left to
